./_drafts/pr-raw/pr-523.txt:38:      "body": "**Actionable comments posted: 20**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (6)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>tsconfig.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-5`: **`@/` 경로 별칭이 정의되었으나 실제로 사용되지 않고 있습니다.**\n\nLine 5의 `\"@/\": [\"./src\"]` 패턴은 기술적으로 `@/foo/bar`와 같은 중첩 경로를 정상적으로 매칭합니다. 그러나 실제 코드베이스에서 `@/`로 시작하는 임포트를 찾을 수 없으므로, 설정은 있지만 활용되지 않는 상태입니다. 또한 `tsconfig.app.json`과 `tsconfig.node.json`에서는 `paths` 속성이 정의되어 있지 않아 IDE 지원이나 타입 체킹 시 일관성 문제가 발생할 수 있습니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@tsconfig.json` at line 5, The tsconfig \"paths\" entry \"@/\": [\"./src\"] is\ndefined but unused and inconsistent across tsconfig.app.json and\ntsconfig.node.json; either remove this unused \"paths\" mapping from tsconfig.json\nor canonicalize it so it actually matches imports (use a wildcard-style mapping\nthat matches \"@/some/path\") and propagate the same \"paths\" configuration into\ntsconfig.app.json and tsconfig.node.json so IDE and type-checking are\nconsistent; search for imports starting with \"@/” to decide whether to remove or\nfix the mapping and then update the \"paths\" key in tsconfig.json plus add the\nidentical \"paths\" section to tsconfig.app.json and tsconfig.node.json.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/core/utils/validator.ts (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-12`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**헬퍼 이름을 프로젝트 규칙에 맞춰 정리해 주세요.**\n\n이 파일은 `**/*.ts` 대상이라 함수/변수명이 snake_case여야 합니다. `isNumericString` / `isValidMonth`는 camelCase이므로, 공개 유틸이라면 이름을 바꾸고 `src/pages/payments/Payments.tsx`의 import도 같이 맞춰 주세요.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/core/utils/validator.ts` around lines 1 - 12, Rename the exported helper\nfunctions from camelCase to snake_case to follow project rules: change\nisNumericString -> is_numeric_string and isValidMonth -> is_valid_month in this\nfile (update both export names and any internal references), and update the\nimport in Payments.tsx that currently imports isNumericString/isValidMonth to\nimport is_numeric_string/is_valid_month instead; ensure all occurrences and\ntests/uses reference the new snake_case identifiers so builds/imports succeed.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/pages/payments/Payments.tsx (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`32-34`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**카드번호 에러 표시를 입력칸별 blur 상태로 좁히는 것을 권장합니다.**\n\n지금은 한 칸만 blur 되어도 다른 미입력 칸까지 바로 에러 스타일이 켜질 수 있습니다. `index`별 blur 상태를 사용하면 피드백 타이밍이 더 자연스럽습니다.\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 151-151\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/pages/payments/Payments.tsx` around lines 32 - 34,\nrenderErrorCardNumberInput currently uses onBlurCardNumber.includes(true) which\ntriggers error styles if any field was blurred; change it to accept an index\n(e.g. renderErrorCardNumberInput(cardNumber: string, index: number)) and use\nonBlurCardNumber[index] && !validateCardNumber(cardNumber) so the error is shown\nonly for the specific input that was blurred; update all call sites of\nrenderErrorCardNumberInput to pass the corresponding index and ensure\nonBlurCardNumber is an array of booleans tracking per-field blur state.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`171-182`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**유효기간도 필드별 blur 기준으로 에러를 분리해 보세요.**\n\n월/년 중 하나만 blur된 시점에 반대 필드까지 즉시 에러 처리되면 조기 경고처럼 보일 수 있습니다. 필드별 blur gating을 적용하면 UX가 더 안정적입니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/pages/payments/Payments.tsx` around lines 171 - 182, 현재 month/ year 입력의\nisError 로직이 Object.values(onBlurExpirationDate).includes(true) 를 사용해 어느 한 필드가\nblur 되면 둘 다 에러 조건을 활성화하고 있습니다; Input 컴포넌트 각각의 isError를 필드별 블러 상태로 게이팅하도록 변경하세요 —\nmonth Input에서는 onBlurExpirationDate.month && !isValidateExpirationDate.month,\nyear Input에서는 onBlurExpirationDate.year && !isValidateExpirationDate.year 를\n사용하도록 바꾸고, 필요하면 handleBlurExpirationDate가 각 필드별 플래그(onBlurExpirationDate.month /\n.year)를 정확히 설정하도록 확인/수정하세요.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/core/components/creditCard/CreditCard.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`11-16`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**`bank` 필드는 현재 사용되지 않으므로 API 정리가 필요합니다.**\n\n필수 props인데 내부에서 읽지 않아 호출부에 불필요한 부담을 줍니다. 지금 단계에서는 `bank`를 제거하거나, 실제 렌더링에 반영하는 방향 중 하나로 정리해 두는 편이 좋습니다.\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 26-31\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/core/components/creditCard/CreditCard.tsx` around lines 11 - 16,\nDefaultCreditCardProps currently includes a bank field that isn't used; either\nremove it from the prop type or use it in rendering. To fix, choose one: (A)\nremove bank: delete bank from the DefaultCreditCardProps interface (and any\nduplicate interface at lines 26-31), remove bank from the CreditCard component's\nprop destructuring/usage, and update all call sites to stop passing bank; or (B)\nuse bank: update the CreditCard component (where DefaultCreditCardProps is\nreferenced) to render or utilize the bank value (e.g., display bank name or\nicon) and ensure prop typing matches. Search for DefaultCreditCardProps and the\nCreditCard component to update types, destructuring, and all callers/tests\naccordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>package.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-13`: **배포 스크립트에서 `gh-pages`를 `devDependencies`에 추가하세요.**\n\n`deploy` 스크립트가 `npx gh-pages -d dist`를 사용하지만 `gh-pages`가 `devDependencies`에 선언되어 있지 않습니다. 이로 인해 실행 시점마다 다른 버전이 설치될 수 있어 CI와 로컬 환경의 재현성이 낮아집니다. `gh-pages`를 의존성에 고정하여 일관된 배포를 보장하세요.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@package.json` at line 13, The deploy script uses npx gh-pages but gh-pages is\nnot declared in package.json; add \"gh-pages\" with a fixed version string to the\npackage.json devDependencies so CI and local environments install the same\nversion, ensuring reproducible deployments; update the devDependencies section\n(referencing the \"deploy\" script name and the \"gh-pages\" package) and run\nyarn/npm install to lock the version in lockfile.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@index.html`:\n- Around line 1-13: The document root declares lang=\"en\" but the app UI is\nKorean; update the HTML root element in index.html by changing the lang\nattribute on the <html> tag from \"en\" to \"ko\" so screen readers and translators\ntreat content as Korean (locate the <html lang=\"en\"> declaration in index.html\nand replace it with lang=\"ko\").\n\nIn `@README.md`:\n- Around line 36-58: The fenced code block in README.md (the block showing the\n/src tree) lacks a language tag and triggers MD040; add a language identifier\n(for example \"text\") immediately after the opening triple backticks so the block\nbecomes ```text ... ``` to satisfy the linter and keep the same content and\nclosing fence intact.\n\nIn `@src/core/components/creditCard/CreditCard.module.css`:\n- Around line 1-7: Remove the unnecessary blank line inside the .creditCard CSS\nrule so declarations are consecutive; edit the .creditCard block (the selector\n.creditCard) to eliminate the empty line between declarations (e.g., after\njustify-content: center;) so the rule no longer triggers the\ndeclaration-empty-line-before lint error.\n\nIn `@src/core/components/formContainer/FormContainer.module.css`:\n- Around line 21-30: Remove the extra blank line before the min-height\ndeclaration inside the .errorMessage rule to satisfy the stylelint rule\ndeclaration-empty-line-before; open FormContainer.module.css, find the\n.errorMessage selector and delete the empty line immediately above the\nmin-height: 20px; declaration so the properties are contiguous and the lint\nwarning disappears.\n\nIn `@src/core/components/formContainer/FormContainer.tsx`:\n- Around line 5-10: The <label> in FormContainer is used without linking to an\ninput; either render a non-label element for static headings or make it a real\nlabel by adding an htmlFor prop: update FormContainerProps to include optional\nhtmlFor?: string, and in FormContainer if htmlFor is provided render <label\nhtmlFor={htmlFor} className={cn(styles.label)}>{label}</label> otherwise render\na <div> or <p> (e.g. <div className={cn(styles.label)}>{label}</div>) so\nsemantics are correct; keep the same styles and existing children/errorMessage\nrendering.\n\nIn `@src/core/components/formGroup/FormGroup.module.css`:\n- Around line 12-38: .titleContainer, .title, .subTitle 규칙에 유효하지 않은 CSS 값들이 있어\nlint가 깨집니다: .title에서 font-style: Bold을 제거(이미 font-weight로 굵기 지정됨)하고\n.title/.subTitle의 letter-spacing: 0%는 허용되지 않으니 0 또는 0px으로 교체하며(stylelint가 요구하는\n단위 형식 준수), stylelint가 지적한 불필요한 빈 줄들을 정리하세요; 변경할 위치 식별에 .titleContainer, .title,\n.subTitle 클래스를 참고하세요.\n\nIn `@src/core/components/formGroup/FormGroup.tsx`:\n- Around line 7-15: The fieldset is missing a legend which harms accessibility;\nupdate the FormGroup component so the title prop is rendered inside a <legend>\n(not a div) and keep subTitle as adjacent helper text (e.g., a div or <p> with\nan accessible class/role) while preserving styling, and ensure FormContainer is\nstill rendered with label, children, and errorMessage; adjust the JSX in the\nFormGroup function (referencing FormGroup, title, subTitle, and FormContainer)\nto move the title into a legend element and retain subTitle as assistive text.\n\nIn `@src/core/components/input/Input.tsx`:\n- Around line 14-24: The Input component currently only toggles visual styles\nvia the isError prop; update the Input (exported Input function) to also expose\nthe semantic invalid state to assistive tech by adding aria-invalid={isError ?\n\"true\" : \"false\"} (and optionally aria-invalid={isError} if boolean is\npreferred) to the rendered <input>, and if there is an associated error message\nhook up aria-describedby when available; ensure the change uses the existing\nisError prop and does not alter other props like value/onChange/onBlur.\n- Around line 4-11: The InputProps interface uses\nReact.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement> but React is not imported; add an import to\nfix type errors—either add a default import (import React from 'react') so\nReact.ChangeEvent works, or change the prop types to use a named type (import\ntype { ChangeEvent } from 'react' and update onChange/onBlur signatures to use\nChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>); update the Input.tsx file where InputProps is\ndeclared to apply one of these fixes.\n\nIn `@src/core/styles/fonts.css`:\n- Line 1: 현재 `@import` 선언에 사용된 URL 'https://googleapis.com'이 잘못되어 폰트가 로드되지 않습니다;\nsrc/core/styles/fonts.css의 `@import` 구문에서 도메인과 경로를 Google Fonts의 올바른 CSS 엔드포인트로\n교체하여 (예: fonts.googleapis.com의 css2 엔드포인트와 적절한 family 쿼리 및 display 옵션을 포함) 올바른\n폰트 CSS를 불러오도록 수정하세요.\n\nIn `@src/core/styles/index.css`:\n- Line 2: The `@import` in src/core/styles/index.css is pulling an incorrect\nfonts.css URL so the body font-family 'Noto Sans' likely falls back to\nsans-serif; update the import in index.css to point to a valid font stylesheet\n(either the correct Google Fonts URL for \"Noto Sans\" or your local/fonts.css\nthat actually contains `@font-face` rules), or add proper `@font-face` declarations\nin src/core/styles/fonts.css so that the body { font-family: 'Noto Sans',\nsans-serif; } will load the font; look for the `@import` \"./fonts.css\" and either\nreplace it with the official Google Fonts link or ensure fonts.css has correct\nsources, formats, and font-display settings for 'Noto Sans'.\n\nIn `@src/core/styles/mordern-normalize.css`:\n- Around line 25-38: The vendored CSS reset triggers stylelint's\ndeclaration-empty-line-before rule for the html rule blocks; either reformat the\nhtml rule in src/core/styles/mordern-normalize.css to satisfy\ndeclaration-empty-line-before (remove/add blank lines so each declaration in the\nhtml { ... } block conforms to the project's rule) or exclude this vendor file\nfrom linting by adding a stylelint ignore (e.g. add the file pattern to\nstylelint.config's ignoreFiles or add an inline disable comment for\ndeclaration-empty-line-before at the top of mordern-normalize.css); reference\nthe html selector block and the declaration-empty-line-before rule when making\nthe change so lint no longer fails.\n\nIn `@src/core/styles/variables.css`:\n- Line 1: 빈 CSS 규칙인 \"body {}\"가 Stylelint의 block-no-empty 규칙을 위반하고 있으므로 해당 빈 블록을\n제거하거나 실제 선언으로 채워 해결하세요; 구체적으로 파일에 있는 \"body {}\" 규칙을 삭제하거나 body 내부에 필요한 스타일 선언(예:\nCSS 변수 선언 또는 다른 속성들)으로 대체하고, 전역 변수라면 :root 또는 기존 변수 파일의 변수명(예:\n--your-variable)으로 옮겨 일관되게 관리하세요.\n\nIn `@src/pages/payments/constant.ts`:\n- Around line 1-4: BRAND_NUMBER currently lists Mastercard BINs only as 51–55,\nmissing the 2221–2720 range; update the BRAND_NUMBER constant (symbol:\nBRAND_NUMBER) so Mastercard includes both the existing\n['51','52','53','54','55'] prefixes and the 2221–2720 range (either by adding\nexplicit string prefixes for the 4-digit range or adding a range representation\nyour validation logic understands, e.g., '2221-2720' or a regex pattern) and\nensure downstream brand-detection logic uses that representation to correctly\nrecognise Mastercard numbers in the 2221–2720 block.\n\nIn `@src/pages/payments/Payments.module.css`:\n- Around line 5-6: Remove the stray blank line before the CSS declaration in\nPayments.module.css to satisfy the declaration-empty-line-before Stylelint rule;\nspecifically delete the empty line immediately preceding the rule containing\n\"max-width: 600px;\" so the declaration directly follows its selector/block\nopening (and re-run Stylelint to confirm the error is resolved).\n\nIn `@src/pages/payments/Payments.tsx`:\n- Around line 108-123: preventCvc currently blocks the empty string and thus\nprevents users from clearing the CVC; also a call to preventCvc in the blur\nhandler is unused. Update preventCvc to explicitly allow '' and otherwise\nenforce isNumericString(value) and value.length <= 3; keep handleChangeCvc using\npreventCvc to gate setCvc. Remove the meaningless call to preventCvc from any\nonBlur handler (or use its boolean result if the blur logic needs it) so\nonBlurCvc/renderErrorMessageCvc and validateCvc can handle empty-value\nvalidation/display correctly.\n\nIn `@src/stories/Configure.mdx`:\n- Around line 37-40: 현재 JSX에서 '# Configure your project' 및 '# Do more with\nStorybook' 같은 마크다운 헤딩 문자열이 일반 텍스트로 렌더링되어 접근성/문서 구조가 손상됩니다; 해당 문자열을 포함하는\ndiv.sb-section-title 블록을 찾아 '# Configure your project'와 '# Do more with\nStorybook' 문자열을 실제 헤딩 요소로 변환(예: <h2 className=\"sb-section-title\">Configure your\nproject</h2> 형태)하고 클래스는 유지하되 내부 텍스트에서 선행 '#'을 제거하여 진짜 헤더 태그로 바꿔주고 동일한 변경을 파일의 다른\n유사 블록(예: 86-90에 해당하는 블록)에도 적용하세요.\n- Line 212: Summary: Fix the typo \"on for\" in the sentence text. Update the\nparagraph string \"Follow guided walkthroughs on for key workflows.\" in\nConfigure.mdx to \"Follow guided walkthroughs for key workflows.\" so the phrase\nreads correctly; locate the exact sentence and replace \"on for\" with \"for\" (the\nparagraph containing \"Follow guided walkthroughs on for key workflows.\").\n- Around line 50-54: Add rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" to every anchor element that\nuses target=\"_blank\" in Configure.mdx (e.g., the <a className=\"sb-action-link\"\nhref=\"...\" target=\"_blank\"> instances such as the one rendering Learn more with\n<RightArrow />) to prevent opener acces